    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0766" n="696" sameAs="frus:frus1883/pg696"/>

                <head>No. 434.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Frelinghuysen to Mr. Cayetano
                        Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1883-06-07"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 7,
                        1883</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note of the 23d ultimo, in relation to the duration of the agreement
                    between the United States and Mexico, providing for the reciprocal crossing of
                    the frontier by troops in pursuit of hostile Indians.</p>
                <p>The understanding of the Department is that the privilege accorded by the
                    agreement of July 29, 1882, ceases after the 18th of August next, pursuant to
                    the subsequent agreement of September 21, 1882, unless the same shall be
                    prolonged by the two Governments.</p>
                <p>Accept, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>FRED’K T. FRELINGHUYSEN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
